Viewing and building this project's documentation
==================================================

Viewing the documentation
--------------------------

The rendered site is committed to this repo -- no build step needed. Just
open it in a browser:

    docs/generated_site/index.html

That's a plain static HTML file, so `file://` opening works fine (there's
no JavaScript-dependent diagram rendering or other network dependency).


Rebuilding the documentation
-----------------------------

Only needed if you've edited a page under `source/`. The build needs
Python 3 and a few packages, all listed in `requirements.txt`.

One-time setup, from this `docs/` directory:

    python3 -m venv .venv
    source .venv/bin/activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt

`pip install` also pulls in the vendored Pygments lexer used for Sitar
syntax highlighting (the `-e ./sitar_pygments_lexer` line inside
`requirements.txt`).

With the venv active, still from `docs/`:

    mkdocs build

The output goes to `generated_site/` -- commit it along with your `.md`
changes so the prebuilt copy stays in sync.


Preview locally while editing
-------------------------------

With the venv active, from `docs/`:

    mkdocs serve

Then open the printed localhost URL in a browser. Pages rebuild live as
you edit `.md` files under `source/`.


Done for the day
------------------

    deactivate
